      "message": "I must be missing something, but I don\u0027t understand how queueDepth\u003d6 is sufficient, with numberOfMessages\u003d300.\n\n- AIUI, we\u0027ll make 300 consecutive calls to sendMessage(), at line 1878. That will cause 300 consecutive calls to answerObj.answer(). I believe these calls happen without any intervening calls to answerObj.process().\n\n- This means that, at the end of the for loop (line 1882), we would need to have 150 packets queued, just for the success case (in expectation).\n\n- But, with queueDepth\u003d6, many of the sendMessage() calls for intended-to-be-successful packets will be answered with FOLLOWUP_TX_QUEUE_FULL, instead.\n\nWhere does my analysis goes wrong?",
